+## Contradiction check (audit focus)
+
+`government/daily-sitting.py::bills_without_ballots()` (lines ~113–120) selects
+every `records/bills/*.md` modified within 21 days that lacks a `.tsv`, without
+any test of bill status. It therefore lists the same three non-eligible files on
+both the 2026-11-17 and 2026-11-18 agendas as though they were pending business.
+This is a transparency defect worth naming: a seat that mechanically obeyed "a
+recorded ballot on each bill above" would fabricate ballot artifacts for bills
+whose sponsors forbade or never solicited a vote, and manufacture a false
+plenary quorum signal. The Clerk's 2026-11-17 record already states there was no
+bill/ballot before the sitting and that ballots would not be fabricated. I treat
+the agenda's bill list as a stale heuristic label, not authority to vote. I do
+**not** change the generator here (that is an Executive/legislative implementation
+matter); I record the contradiction for audit.
